{{- /*
  github/shared/pr-fetch-review-threads — fetch every unresolved (and
  not-outdated) review thread for a PR via GraphQL, producing a THREADS_JSON
  array whose length is the unresolved-comment count.

  `gh pr view --json reviewThreads` does NOT exist — the field is GraphQL-only.

  Callers: babysit-this-pr §3c, babysit-my-prs §3d.

  Placeholders substituted by the agent from the surrounding context:
    <owner>/<repo> — the target repository (e.g. "some-org/some-repo")
    <number>       — the PR number
*/ -}}
`gh pr view --json reviewThreads` is **not supported** by the `gh` CLI — the
field only exists via GraphQL. Fetch unresolved threads with `gh api graphql`:

```bash
# Every unresolved (and not-outdated) review thread with the first comment
# of each thread (author, path, line, body, thread id).
REPO_OWNER=$(echo "<owner>/<repo>" | cut -d/ -f1)
REPO_NAME=$(echo "<owner>/<repo>" | cut -d/ -f2)
gh api graphql -f query='
query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
    pullRequest(number:$number) {
      reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes {
        id isResolved isOutdated
        comments(first:1) { nodes {
          author { login } path line originalLine body
        } }
      } }
    }
  }
}' -F owner="$REPO_OWNER" -F name="$REPO_NAME" -F number=<number> \
  --jq '[.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]
         | select(.isResolved == false and .isOutdated == false)
         | {id, path: .comments.nodes[0].path,
            line: (.comments.nodes[0].line // .comments.nodes[0].originalLine),
            author: .comments.nodes[0].author.login,
            body: .comments.nodes[0].body}]'
```

Save the JSON array as `THREADS_JSON`. Its length is the unresolved count; if
zero, there is nothing to address.
